/// @file build_scripts.dox
/// @brief Build and documentation workflow reference
///
/// This file documents the repository's Windows build helper and the equivalent
/// CMake commands. The helper is implemented in @ref build.ps1, and the build
/// and documentation targets are declared in @ref CMakeLists.txt.
///
/// @section build_ps1 Windows build helper
///
/// Run `build.ps1` from PowerShell at the repository root:
///
/// @code{.powershell}
/// ./build.ps1
/// @endcode
///
/// The script formats the top-level C++ source files under `src/`, configures the
/// `windows` CMake preset when the Ninja build files or compilation database are
/// missing, builds the preset in parallel, and runs `clang-tidy` on those C++
/// source files using `build/compile_commands.json`. A formatting, build, or
/// clang-tidy failure stops the script with an error.
///
/// The script requires CMake 4.4 or newer. CMake, `clang-format`, and
/// `clang-tidy` must be available on `PATH`. The Windows preset also requires
/// Ninja, `clang-cl`, and a Vulkan SDK with `glslc`.
///
/// @section cmake_build Manual CMake build
///
/// To configure and build without the PowerShell helper, run:
///
/// @code{.powershell}
/// cmake --preset windows
/// cmake --build --preset windows --parallel
/// @endcode
///
/// @section docs_build Generate documentation
///
/// When Doxygen is installed, generate the HTML reference with either command:
///
/// @code{.powershell}
/// doxygen Doxyfile
/// @endcode
///
/// @code{.powershell}
/// cmake --build --preset windows --target docs
/// @endcode
///
/// The generated reference is written to `build/docs/html/index.html`.
